{"text": " If I had to raise prices on customers tomorrow, this is the letter that I would send them. So my price raise letters have five sections and I use the acronym RAISE to remember it. So R stands for remind them of the value they've gotten. A is address the price trades directly. So don't try and like hide it somewhere like be upfront. I is invest in their future. Basically frame the price increase in the context of the value that you're gonna keep investing in to help them out. S is soften the news with a loyalty discount that expires in three to six months from now. And then E, explain away their concerns with a PS statement at the bottom of the letter. And so this is what it looks like when it's all together. If this sounds interesting, follow for more free stuff.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 2.04, "text": " If I had to raise prices on customers tomorrow,", "tokens": [50364, 759, 286, 632, 281, 5300, 7901, 322, 4581, 4153, 11, 50466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09116459929424783, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 0.0049660298973321915}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 2.04, "end": 3.36, "text": " this is the letter that I would send them.", "tokens": [50466, 341, 307, 264, 5063, 300, 286, 576, 2845, 552, 13, 50532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09116459929424783, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 0.0049660298973321915}, {"id": 2, "seek": 0, "start": 3.36, "end": 5.24, "text": " So my price raise letters have five sections", "tokens": [50532, 407, 452, 3218, 5300, 7825, 362, 1732, 10863, 50626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09116459929424783, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 0.0049660298973321915}, {"id": 3, "seek": 0, "start": 5.24, "end": 7.16, "text": " and I use the acronym RAISE to remember it.", "tokens": [50626, 293, 286, 764, 264, 39195, 14626, 19413, 281, 1604, 309, 13, 50722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09116459929424783, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_